    given-names: "Contributors"
title: "DR-QFormer: Parameter-Efficient Middleware for RAG"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2025-10-29
url: "https://github.com/gugupig/DR-QFormer"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gugupig/DR-QFormer"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - RAG
  - Q-Former
  - parameter-efficient
  - BLIP-2
  - natural-language-processing
  - machine-learning
abstract: |
  DR-QFormer is a BLIP-2-style parameter-efficient middleware for 
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). It uses learnable query tokens 
  in a Q-Former architecture to bridge frozen retrievers and frozen 
  large language models, training only the Q-Former and task-specific 
  heads while keeping retrieval and generation components frozen.
